pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Truth: SATISFIABLE. Both rows have a left-hand side in [0,3] and a hugely
% NEGATIVE right-hand side, so both are trivially true. `sat.pbp` here makes
% the same checker say `s VERIFIED SATISFIABLE`, with the model x1 = x2 = 0.
%
% Same defect as fixture 11 in the OTHER file: not all coefficients are 1, so
% these rows are stored as `GeneralPBConstraint<i64>` and the addition runs
% `GeneralPBConstraint::add` (general_pb_constraint.rs) instead of
% `Cardinality::add`. That function has the same shape: it validates that the
% summed degree fits into `N` and then does `set_degree(degree_sum -
% &cancellation)` in `N`. A fix applied only to cardinality.rs still fails here.
%
% `pol 1 2 +`: the degrees sum to exactly i64::MIN; 2 x1 and 2 ~x1 cancel by 2.
% Correct result:  `2 x2 >= -9223372036854775810`   (trivially true)
% Unfixed result:  `2 x2 >= 9223372036854775806`    (degree above the
%                   coefficient sum 2, i.e. a contradiction)
% so `conclusion UNSAT : 3` is accepted.
f 2 ;
pol 1 2 + ;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT : 3 ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
